description: The door into this repository

! TW5-Syntax

A TextMate grammar for TiddlyWiki wikitext and the memetic dialect, and the instruments that hold
it to the parser it answers to.

!! What this wiki holds

|!Kind |!What it answers |!How it stays true |
|''judgement'' |a question no registry answers, which a person weighs |argued here, gated against what the host documents |
|''harvest'' |what the installed TiddlyWiki knows |written by a boot, never by a hand |

The two look alike — both JSON data tiddlers — and they fail differently. A judgement goes stale
when the world moves and nobody notices. A harvest goes stale on a version, and says so.

|!Tiddler |!Kind |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/BuiltInVariables">> |judgement — which names TiddlyWiki's core owns |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/ReaderRelations">> |judgement — what a reader must meet as one, and what a reader must tell apart |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/PlainConstructs">> |judgement — why a construct reads as prose rather than as a thing |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/GrammarSignals">> |harvest — every filter operator, widget and wikitext rule this TiddlyWiki registers |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/CIGates">> |judgement — which gates continuous integration runs, and the reason for each one it does not |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/GateReport">> |harvest — what every gate said when it last ran |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/EditionBuild">> |harvest — the compiler that built the edition's modules, and the sources they answer to |

Each judgement carries its own reason beside it. A reason belongs with the ruling it explains, and
a comment in a tool keeps it where nobody weighs it — so the wiki shows both, and a reason that
stops answering to anything fails the gate that reads it, the same way a missing ruling does.

!! What continuous integration runs

Every witness the manifest names, CI runs — or <<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/CIGates">> carries the
reason it does not. Three kinds stand there:

|!kind |!what it means |
|''run'' |the gate blocks a merge |
|''reporting'' |the gate answers to a TiddlyWiki this repository does not pin, so upstream moving reports rather than blocks |
|''skipped'' |a ruling names what stands in the way, and the specification lives beside it |

`tools/ci-runs-the-gates.test.js` holds the workflow to that list rather than to a copy of it. A
gate added to the manifest joins without anybody remembering, and a reason that stops answering to
anything — a ruling for a gate CI runs anyway — fails the same way a missing one does.

!! Running a gate from here

The wiki that shows a ruling runs the instrument that enforces it:

```
tiddlywiki editions/tw5-syntax --gate list
tiddlywiki editions/tw5-syntax --gate colour-witness dark-construct
tiddlywiki editions/tw5-syntax --gate
```

The command stands in this wiki as <<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/modules/grammar-commands">>, so a
reader who wants to know what it does opens it rather than a file beside the wiki. Its gate list
comes from the manifest by way of the report, so one added joins without anybody remembering.

!! How a new TiddlyWiki reaches the grammar

# `npm run signals` boots this edition against the TiddlyWiki the repo answers to, and writes what it found.
# `npm run rule-coverage` holds the grammar to it: every wikitext rule the host stands, the grammar reads — under its own name, or under one a line declares.
# `npm run builtins -- --check` holds the grammar to the judgement beside it.
# A rule the host added and the grammar never learned fails the second step, so a version bump arrives as a failing gate rather than as a construct that quietly reads as prose.

Nothing in that chain edits the grammar for you. It reports what a release changed and stops, so
an operator decides what the change means.

!! The repository, readable here

Five directories load into this wiki as tiddlers, read from where those files sit rather than
copied. A `tiddlywiki.files` spec beside each one names the directory. Open a tiddler and the
source stands there, comments and all; edit the file on disk and the next boot shows the edit.

|!Directory |!Prefix |!Tag |
|`tools/` |`$:/tw5-syntax/tools/` |`$:/tags/TW5Syntax/Tool` for an instrument, `ToolTest` for the test beside it |
|`syntaxes/` |`$:/tw5-syntax/syntaxes/` |`$:/tags/TW5Syntax/Grammar` |
|`snippets/` |`$:/tw5-syntax/snippets/` |`$:/tags/TW5Syntax/Snippet` |
|`docs/` |`$:/tw5-syntax/docs/` |`$:/tags/TW5Syntax/Meme`, and `PriorArt` for the survey |
|`tests/` |`$:/tw5-syntax/tests/` |`Assertion`, `Specimen`, `Snapshot`, `TestFixture`, `KnownGap` |

The memes under `docs/` load as wikitext and render. Everything under `tests/` loads as plain
text on purpose: a specimen exists for a tokenizer rather than for a reader, and rendering one shows
what the construct means instead of the characters the assertion pins.

<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/Corpus">> names the one directory that stays outside, and why.

!!! One home for the instruments

An instrument and the test that collides it sit in the same directory: `tools/theme-model.js`
beside `tools/theme-model.test.js`.

Splitting them across two directories named `tools` promises a mirror that measurement refuses. Of
the 29 tests in this repository, 15 answer a question about the whole repository rather than about
any instrument, and 14 instruments carry no test under their own name. A reader who trusts such a
name looks for a pairing that stands for half the files.

So each directory holds one kind of thing. `tests/` holds the grammar assertions: declarative, read
by `vscode-tmgrammar-test`, one directory per dialect, with the vendored grammars they resolve
against under `tests/grammars/`. `tools/` holds the executable ones, which `node --test` runs. Each
answers to its own runner, and the directory says which.

The wiki reads both from the one directory and tells them apart by tag — `Tool` for an instrument,
`ToolTest` for a test — so a reader browsing the instruments meets no test, and a reader after a
test finds it beside what it collides.

!!! Two hazards a spec carries

A `tiddlywiki.files` REPLACES the scan of the directory holding it. One dropped beside the
edition's own tiddlers stopped it loading them — the harvest went silent and the signals gate said
so within the minute. Every spec here sits in a subdirectory of its own, holding nothing but
itself, so it replaces a scan that would have found nothing.

A `.meta` sidecar outranks a spec. The loader hard-excludes `*.meta`, and merges the sidecar's
fields over the ones the spec asks for, so a sidecar carrying `title:` names the tiddler and the
prefix loses. `tests/samples/tiddlywiki5.tw` arrives as `$:/wikitext.tw` because the malformed
fixture beside it says so, which names the reason that fixture stands. The gate holds that shape by
deriving it — a pair on disk, neither half under the house prefix — rather than by naming the
file, so a specimen that grows a sidecar gets covered without anybody remembering.

<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/tools/wiki-reads-the-repo.test.js">> boots the edition and compares
every arriving tiddler against the bytes on disk, so a spec that stops reaching a file, or a file
that reaches the wiki changed, fails rather than goes quiet.

!! Where the rest stands

|!Surface |!What it carries |
|`syntaxes/` |the grammars — one wikitext base, one dialect, two injections registered to both |
|`tests/` |the grammar assertions — declarative, read by `vscode-tmgrammar-test`, one dialect per directory |
|`tests/samples/` |specimens, and the snapshots `npm run snap-update` re-pins |
|`tools/` |the witnesses, and the test beside each one that collides it against the fault it stands for |
|`docs/prior-art/` |twenty highlighting systems surveyed, kept verbatim |
|`tests/grammars/` |grammars other people wrote, so an embedded-language assertion resolves the scope it names |
|`corpus/` |broad ground, gated on invariants — on disk, never in the wiki |
